-- title:
--   Multiplicity one mod 𝔪 for the ordinary multiplicative part
-- statement:
--   Fix an odd prime $p$ and an integer $M\neq 0$ with $p\mid M$ and $p^2\nmid M$, and a subgroup $H\le(\mathbb Z/M)^\times$ containing every unit whose image under reduction $(\mathbb Z/M)^\times\to(\mathbb Z/(M/p))^\times$ is $1$. Assume given $d\in(\mathbb Z/M)^\times$ whose image in $\mathbb Z/(M/p)$ is the class of $p$, and such that this image, or its negative, lies in [`ModularCurve.infSubgroup p M H hpM`](def/ModularCurve_XHDifferentialsModL.html#L246), the image of $H$ in $(\mathbb Z/(M/p))^\times$. Let $S$ be a finite set of primes-to-be-excluded, and assume [`ModularCurve.HeckeDiamondInputsHAll M H`](def/ModularCurve_XHOperators.html#L113): the Hecke input data `HeckeInputsHAlong` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ hold at every prime $\ell$, and every $d\in(\mathbb Z/M)^\times$ is realised by an automorphism of `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ satisfying `IsDiamondAutHBar`. Let $T=$ [`TateModule p (ModularCurve.JH M H)`](def/EllipticCurve_TateModule.html#L15), the group of sequences $(x_n)$ in the degree-zero divisor class group of `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` with $p^nx_n=0$ and $px_{n+1}=x_n$. Let $\mathbb T$ be a commutative $\mathbb Z_p$-algebra acting on $T$ compatibly with the $\mathbb Z_p$-action and faithfully (any $t$ killing all of $T$ is $0$), and let $op$ assign to each generator symbol $g$ in [`CohCarrier.Gen M S`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L13) — $T_\ell$ for $\ell$ prime, $\ell\notin S$, $\ell\nmid M$; $U_q$ for $q$ prime dividing $M$; $\langle d\rangle$ for $d\in(\mathbb Z/M)^\times$ — an element of $\mathbb T$ acting on $T$ as the endomorphism [`ModularCurve.tateGenOpH M H S p g`](def/ModularCurve_XHOperators.html#L99), the range of $op$ generating $\mathbb T$ as a $\mathbb Z_p$-algebra. Let $S'$ be an [`IharaLemma.IdempotentSplitting`](def/IharaLemma_IdempotentSplitting.html#L7) of $\mathbb T$: a complete orthogonal family of idempotents $e_i$ together with maximal ideals $\mathfrak m_i$ exhausting the maximal ideals of $\mathbb T$ and satisfying $e_i\in\mathfrak m_j\iff i\neq j$. Fix an index $i_0$, a field $k$ of characteristic $p$, a ring homomorphism $\pi_k$ from the corner ring at $e_{i_0}$ to $k$, and $\bar\theta:$ [`CohCarrier.Gen M S`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L13) $\to k$ with $\pi_k(e_{i_0}\,op(g)\,e_{i_0})=\bar\theta(g)$. Assume ordinarity $\bar\theta(U_p)\neq0$ and non-Eisensteinness: some prime $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid M$ and $\ell\equiv1\pmod M$ has $\bar\theta(T_\ell)\neq\ell+1$ in $k$. Let $P_l$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $p$ in its non-units, and let $P_0$ be the $\mathbb T$-submodule of $T$ consisting of the $x$ lying in the corner submodule $e_{i_0}\cdot T$ and satisfying $\sigma x=\chi_{\mathrm{cyc},p}(\sigma)\,x$ for all $\sigma$ in the inertia subgroup of $P_l$ over $\mathbb Q$, where $\sigma$ acts through [`ModularCurve.JH.tateGaloisRep`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L154). Then there is $x_0\in P_0$ such that every $x\in P_0$ satisfies $x-t\,x_0\in\mathfrak m_{i_0}P_0$ for some $t\in\mathbb T$; that is, $P_0$ is generated by a single element modulo $\mathfrak m_{i_0}P_0$.
--
--   This is the multiplicity one assertion for the multiplicative (inertia-cyclotomic) part of the $p$-adic Tate module of $J_H(M)$ at an ordinary non-Eisenstein maximal ideal, with $p$ exactly dividing $M$ and the class of $p$ lying in $\pm H'$, in the form of Wiles' Chapter 2 results on ordinary deformation rings. It feeds the companion statement producing an actual $\mathbb T$-module generator of the corner submodule, and hence the freeness of rank one statements used in the Taylor–Wiles argument.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_forall_sub_smul_mem_maximalIdeal_smul_multiplicativeSubmodule_tateModule_jH_of_ordinary_of_not_isEisenstein_of_mem_infSubgroup.lean

